               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 62-year-old male admitted on 25/06/2022 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. Spirometry confirmed severely reduced airflow. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and antibiotic coverage. Clinical response was satisfactory, and oxygen saturation normalised prior to discharge. He has been advised on inhaler technique and exacerbation action plan. Please arrange follow-up spirometry and COPD review within four weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
